{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c64f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07545-b24a-7111-bd71-a49bf0fc5a97"},"sequence":386,"recorded_at":1780531400000767,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e61bb3fc-6388-408f-a265-e94b890e4ba1","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e61bb3fc-6388-408f-a265-e94b890e4ba1","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e61bb3fc-6388-408f-a265-e94b890e4ba1"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"b270bda4-aa48-4155-ad21-639de6d0771e"},"task_id":"b270bda4-aa48-4155-ad21-639de6d0771e","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"b270bda4-aa48-4155-ad21-639de6d0771e","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3drr2m/worktree/internal/sessadapter/inventory_test.go`.\n1|package sessadapter\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"fmt\"\n5|\t\"go/ast\"\n6|\t\"go/parser\"\n7|\t\"go/token\"\n8|\t\"os\"\n9|\t\"path/filepath\"\n10|\t\"sort\"\n11|\t\"strconv\"\n12|\t\"strings\"\n13|\t\"testing\"\n14|)\n15|\n16|// This file is the derived refusal-arm inventory. It exists\n17|// because a new refusal through an existing site — a widened\n18|// member set, a new detail literal, a dropped check that slides\n19|// to a lower arm — leaves the whole suite green unless the arm\n20|// set is derived from production source by parsing it, never by\n21|// listing it.\n22|//\n23|// Derivation (deriveRefusalArms): every call to one of the seven\n24|// refusal constructors with a string-literal first argument\n25|// yields ctor|<constructor>|<detail>; a call whose first\n26|// argument is a literal prefix plus fault.detail yields\n27|// ctor|<constructor>|conduit|<function>|<prefix>, so conduits in\n28|// different functions never merge; every &frameFault{...}\n29|// literal yields frame|<detail>. A constructor call with any\n30|// other first-argument shape lands as\n31|// ctor|<constructor>|expr|<function> rather than passing\n32|// silently. Constructor references outside direct-call position\n33|// fail the derivation outright: an aliased constructor hides\n34|// every arm it builds. All three alias spellings are caught —\n35|// `alias := failInvalid`, `var alias = failInvalid` at package\n36|// level, and `var alias = failInvalid` inside a function body —\n37|// because the gate exempts only the definition's own Name in its\n38|// ValueSpec, never a constructor identifier appearing as a\n39|// ValueSpec value. The constructors of this package are\n40|// themselves declared as `var failX = func...`, so their\n41|// definition Names must stay exempt while any other var-held\n42|// reference fails.\n43|// Package-level var initializers scan under their variable name,\n44|// so a refusal arm hiding in a package-level func literal is\n45|// derived, not missed.\n46|//\n47|// The constructor denominator is itself derived, not listed on\n48|// trust: TestRefusalConstructorsMatchProduction requires the\n49|// registered set to equal the package-level vars whose bodies\n50|// call axerror.New, every axerror.New site in production to sit\n51|// inside one registered body, and no func-value indirection of\n52|// axerror.New anywhere. An eighth constructor, an inline\n53|// axerror.New refusal, or a `var newFault = axerror.New`\n54|// indirection carries an additive arm the derivation never\n55|// observes, and fails there instead of passing silently.\n56|//\n57|// Both directions are checked:\n58|// TestDerivedRefusalArmsAreAllWitnessed (every derived arm\n59|// carries a witness) and TestWitnessedArmsAreAllDerived (every\n60|// witness names a derived arm, so a truncated derivation reddens\n61|// on the orphaned witnesses instead of passing vacuously).\n62|// TestEveryArmWitnessRefusesAtTheProductionEntry drives each\n63|// witness through the production entry and requires the refusal\n64|// to come from the arm under test: code, distinguishing detail,\n65|// and rule text. Empty, single-file, or unparseable derivations\n66|// fail closed: a domain that silently derives nothing is not a\n67|// measurement.\n68|//\n69|// Stated bounds: the five timestamp pairs share one\n70|// (constructor, detail) identity across their checkTimestamp and\n71|// Time halves by construction (one rule, two halves); deleting\n72|// one half is a behavioral mutant the entry-point tests must\n73|// catch, and every witness below proves both halves. Arms\n74|// sharing one identity merge to one obligation only there and\n75|// nowhere else: any other merge fails the derivation. The\n76|// open-class member gates (unknown-member and duplicate-member\n77|// refusals) range over an unbounded name class, so one witness\n78|// per arm proves the gate fires, not that every name is gated:\n79|// a mutant exempting a different name than the witnessed one is\n80|// outside what the arm inventory narrows, and is recorded here\n81|// rather than proven.\n82|//\n83|// Shape space (review rev6 G-B; the brief asked what shape comes\n84|// after the one just closed, so the answer is written here). An\n85|// error construction in this package can only be carried by\n86|// these AST shapes; the census derives or refuses each one:\n87|//\n88|//   1. A direct `failX(...)` call — DERIVED as an arm keyed by\n89|//      the literal detail (or conduit/expr shape).\n90|//   2. A package-level `var failY = func...` literal whose body\n91|//      calls axerror.New — DERIVED as a constructor: the\n92|//      produced set must equal refusalConstructors exactly, so\n93|//      an eighth constructor fails as unregistered.\n94|//   3. An axerror.New call outside every registered literal\n95|//      (inline in a function, in a function-local literal even\n96|//      under a registered name) — REFUSED as a construction\n97|//      site outside the registered bodies.\n98|//   4. An axerror.New selector in non-call position (alias var,\n99|//      returned constructor, argument, struct field) — REFUSED\n100|//      as a func-value indirection (the import census pins the\n101|//      `axerror` binding it matches on).\n102|//   5. A failX identifier in non-call, non-definition position\n103|//      (alias var/:=, assignment, argument, return, struct\n104|//      field, method value) — REFUSED as a constructor alias\n105|//      that would bury every arm built through it (proven per\n106|//      position by TestConstructorAliasSpellingsFailDerivation).\n107|//   6. An import of the error package path under any other name\n108|//      — REFUSED by the import census\n109|//      (TestAxerrorImportsAreUnaliased pins the `axerror`\n110|//      binding every identifier match above relies on).\n111|//   7. A &frameFault{...} literal — DERIVED as a frame arm by\n112|//      its type name and literal detail.\n113|//\n114|// 7 of 7 shapes derived-or-refused, each with a synthetic proof.\n115|// The residue, stated here rather than left silent: a frameFault\n116|// built through a type alias (`type ff = frameFault`) would hide\n117|// from shape 7 — no such alias exists in production; a\n118|// construction via assembly, linkname, or reflect would hide\n119|// from shapes 3-4 — the package uses none of those mechanisms;\n120|// files outside the package directory and _test.go files, which\n(more lines below)"}}}
