{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c7f7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07545-b24a-7111-bd71-a49bf0fc5a97"},"sequence":598,"recorded_at":1780531400001191,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e61bb3fc-6388-408f-a265-e94b890e4ba1","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e61bb3fc-6388-408f-a265-e94b890e4ba1","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e61bb3fc-6388-408f-a265-e94b890e4ba1"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"a658de65-7ecc-4318-9778-a4bde985c7ac"},"task_id":"a658de65-7ecc-4318-9778-a4bde985c7ac","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"a658de65-7ecc-4318-9778-a4bde985c7ac","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3drr2m/worktree/internal/axerror/axerror.go`.\n1|// Package axerror implements the AX Structured Error contract of pinned\n2|// specification Sections 15.1 through 15.3: the closed versioned failure\n3|// object, its stable code-to-exit registry, its retryability rule, its typed\n4|// diagnostic details, and the redaction that keeps a local cause off the wire.\n5|//\n6|// The package holds no state, opens no file, and starts no process. It\n7|// advertises no provider, platform, backend, or CLI capability, and mutates no\n8|// durable state, so it has no crash or idempotency surface of its own.\n9|package axerror\n10|\n11|import (\n12|\t\"bytes\"\n13|\t\"encoding/json\"\n14|\t\"errors\"\n15|\t\"fmt\"\n16|\t\"unicode/utf8\"\n17|\n18|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n19|)\n20|\n21|// ErrInvalidStructuredError reports a failure object outside the closed Section\n22|// 15.1 shape.\n23|var ErrInvalidStructuredError = errors.New(\"invalid structured error\")\n24|\n25|// IDs carries the two optional Section 15.1 identifiers. The pinned document\n26|// says they \"are optional and MUST be present when known\", which is an\n27|// obligation on the constructing call site rather than a shape a validator can\n28|// check. This type turns the obligation into a decision the call site has to\n29|// make: NoIDs states that neither identifier is known, and WithOperation and\n30|// WithSession state that one is. There is no way to leave the question\n31|// unanswered by forgetting a struct field.\n32|type IDs struct {\n33|\toperation *scalar.UUIDv7\n34|\tsession   *scalar.UUIDv7\n35|}\n36|\n37|// NoIDs states that no operation was allocated and the failure is not\n38|// session-scoped.\n39|func NoIDs() IDs { return IDs{} }\n40|\n41|// WithOperation records an allocated operation identifier.\n42|func (ids IDs) WithOperation(operation scalar.UUIDv7) IDs {\n43|\tids.operation = &operation\n44|\treturn ids\n45|}\n46|\n47|// WithSession records the session the failure is scoped to.\n48|func (ids IDs) WithSession(session scalar.UUIDv7) IDs {\n49|\tids.session = &session\n50|\treturn ids\n51|}\n52|\n53|// Operation reports the allocated operation identifier, if one is known.\n54|func (ids IDs) Operation() (scalar.UUIDv7, bool) {\n55|\tif ids.operation == nil {\n56|\t\treturn scalar.UUIDv7{}, false\n57|\t}\n58|\treturn *ids.operation, true\n59|}\n60|\n61|// Session reports the session the failure is scoped to, if one is known.\n62|func (ids IDs) Session() (scalar.UUIDv7, bool) {\n63|\tif ids.session == nil {\n64|\t\treturn scalar.UUIDv7{}, false\n65|\t}\n66|\treturn *ids.session, true\n67|}\n68|\n69|// Spec is the complete input to New. It deliberately has no exit-code field:\n70|// the exit status is resolved from the pinned registry for the selected\n71|// version, so a call site cannot mint a mapping the specification does not\n72|// assign, and no reviewer has to check one against the table by hand.\n73|type Spec struct {\n74|\t// Version is the Structured Error version the containing contract binds.\n75|\tVersion Version\n76|\t// Code is a stable registry code the selected version registers.\n77|\tCode Code\n78|\t// Message is human text of 1..4096 UTF-8 characters. Automation never\n79|\t// branches on it.\n80|\tMessage string\n81|\t// Retryable is true only when the identical request may safely be retried\n82|\t// without new authority or confirmation.\n83|\tRetryable bool\n84|\t// IDs carries the operation and session identifiers that are known.\n85|\tIDs IDs\n86|\t// Details is the required diagnostic map. An empty map is valid; nil is\n87|\t// not, because the member itself is required.\n88|\tDetails Details\n89|\t// Cause is the local Go error this failure was built from. It is kept for\n90|\t// errors.Is and errors.As and is structurally unreachable from the wire\n91|\t// object: no encoder in this package can serialize it.\n92|\tCause error\n93|}\n94|\n95|// Error is one validated Structured Error. Every field is unexported and the\n96|// only encoder is MarshalJSON, so the closed Section 15.1 object is the only\n97|// shape this type can produce and the local cause cannot escape into it.\n98|//\n99|// The details map is owned outright rather than shared. New deep-copies the\n100|// caller's map on the way in and Detail deep-copies on the way out, so the\n101|// graph ValidateDetails checked is the graph this object encodes. A shallow\n102|// copy would leave every Section 15.1 detail bound - the four forbidden\n103|// classes, the 16 KiB canonical size, the depth-4 nesting limit, the admitted\n104|// value types - violable after construction through a retained nested\n105|// container, which is a bypass path around the gate rather than a gate.\n106|type Error struct {\n107|\tversion   Version\n108|\tcode      Code\n109|\tmessage   string\n110|\texitCode  int\n111|\tretryable bool\n112|\tids       IDs\n113|\tdetails   Details\n114|\tcause     error\n115|\n116|\t// codeRegistered records whether the pinned registry carries this code for\n117|\t// this version. It is false only for an object decoded from a conforming\n118|\t// peer that used a code added in a later compatible minor.\n119|\tcodeRegistered bool\n120|}\n121|\n122|// New builds a Structured Error from spec. It refuses, in this order: an\n123|// unregistered version; a code the version does not register; a message outside\n124|// 1..4096 UTF-8 characters; a details map outside the Section 15.1 bounds or\n125|// carrying a Section 16.2 excluded class; a code whose typed details the pinned\n126|// document names and spec omits; a retryable claim the pinned document\n127|// forbids; and human text or a detail value that reproduces the local cause\n128|// verbatim.\n129|//\n130|// The exit status is never taken from the caller. It is resolved through\n(more lines below)"}}}
