{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e089","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07545-b24a-7111-bd71-a49bf0fc5a97"},"sequence":3743,"recorded_at":1780531400007481,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e61bb3fc-6388-408f-a265-e94b890e4ba1","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e61bb3fc-6388-408f-a265-e94b890e4ba1","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e61bb3fc-6388-408f-a265-e94b890e4ba1"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"b7bba32e-e58c-4c00-81aa-908eb86e3124"},"task_id":"b7bba32e-e58c-4c00-81aa-908eb86e3124","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"b7bba32e-e58c-4c00-81aa-908eb86e3124","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-117-1\",\n  \"command\": \"ls ~/.claude/skills/logbook/ 2>/dev/null; grep -n \\\"logbook\\\" LOGBOOK.md | head -n 3; head -n 30 LOGBOOK.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Check repo logbook convention\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"README.md\\nSKILL.md\\n45:- SCOPE: TASK-260830-32jeti round-6 verdict (changes requested, two blocking findings F1/F2 plus the nondeterministic suite). Carries the reviewer's findings into the logbook — the reviewer deliberately left LOGBOOK.md out of their delta. Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\\n170:- NOTE: the rev1 verdict supplied a complete logbook entry with an instruction to land it verbatim, and `LOGBOOK.md` is untouched in `292fc6d..d8fc669`. The lesson that would have prevented this round's omission was written into a board resource and never reached the file the next round reads. A verdict-supplied entry is part of the rework scope, not an appendix to it.\\n340:### 0742 — A key-name blacklist, again: the same shape BUG-260902-2faftr removed, caught by reading the logbook rather than by a test\\n# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-06\\n\\n### 0618 — Session-adapter leaf round-4 rework: rev3 B4/B5/B6 closed as classes, N6 fixed in code\\n\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-2z3se0 round-4 rework (review-verdict-rev3, changes requested, B4–B6 blocking + N6). Test-only additions inside `internal/sessadapter/` (`zero_absent_test.go`, `bounds_edge_test.go`, `import_census_test.go`) plus a two-line production-test fix in `inventory_test.go` and this entry. No production behavior change; the 323-arm inventory floor is untouched. Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\\n- FIX (B4): the zero/absent-fact class is now derived, not listed. `TestEnvelopeEchoEmptyStringRefuses` iterates the echo members from the production Required slices (request [:2], success/failure [:4] = 10 rows) with wants from `ProtocolID`/`ProtocolVersion`/`wantRequest()`, each driven as `\\\"\\\"` through its entry point; `TestCheckTargetWriteGatesAbsentAdapterRefuses` deletes each required adapter name (set derived from `DoctorRequiredCapabilities`) and both writers together; `TestCapabilityUsableAbsentIsNotUsable` deletes every `capabilityOrder` name through both `CapabilityUsable` and `capabilityMapUsable`; `TestCheckDoctorHealthyRefusesEmptyRequiredName` pins the name gate against `\\\"\\\"`.\\n- FIX (B5): `TestStringBoundEdges` (17 rows: all 16 survivor `checkStringBounds` maxima plus probe detail 0..2048) drives min-1/min/max/max+1 through the entry; `TestArrayBoundEdges` drives 0/1/max/max+1 for argv count, disposition lists, contract rows, and versions. Same-width sortable fixtures where the gate orders members (zero-padded `c01..c64` contract ids, `1.0.0-a01..a33` prerelease versions); the 8-entry disposition refusal lands on the count arm because it fires before the element gates.\\n- FIX (B6): new `TestAxerrorImportsAreUnaliased` — every production import of the error path must bind `axerror` (default or identical alias); renamed, blank, and dot bindings fail, with a zero-importer fail-closed guard. The constructor census is now sound as written without special-casing aliases. Synthetic alias vectors prove the gate shape.\\n- FIX (N6): `constructorSitesInFile` now reports the function-local registered-name case (`case !topLevel`, was a silent fall-through), matching its comment; pinned by synthetic `TestConstructorSitesReportFunctionLocalRegisteredName` (reports locally, stays exempt at package level).\\n- EVIDENCE: narrowing-mutant battery 36/36 killed, 0 survived — exactly the reviewer's 35 survivors (10 envelope + 3 presence + 20 bounds + 2 alias) plus the N6 arm. Every mutant grep-confirmed present and `go vet`-clean before its verdict; tree sha-verified identical after. A3/A4 additionally hold the constructor census green, so the kill comes from the import census, not the floor. Harness lesson: piped `go test | tail` reports tail's exit 0 — the first battery run showed 0/36 for that reason; all gate statuses here are unpiped direct exit codes.\\n- GATES: `go build ./...` 0, `go vet ./...` 0, `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` 0, gofmt clean, `go test ./...` 17/17 exit 0 (sessadapter 976 PASS/0 FAIL, cover 81.5%), `-race` on sessadapter exit 0, `tracecheck` exit 0 (acceptance_cases=88, unchanged — no behavior change, no new AC rows).\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off uncommitted.\\n\\n### 0515 — Session-adapter leaf round-3 rework: rev2 B1–B3 closed, N4/N5 closed-or-bounded\\n\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-2z3se0 round-3 rework (review-verdict-rev2, changes requested, B1–B3 blocking + N4/N5). All changes inside `internal/sessadapter/` except this entry. Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\\n- FIX (B1): `checkValidateResult` no longer calls `checkValidateNullability` — the pinned §7.8 validate success member list names no target members, so the request-body nullability rule cannot apply to successes. Archive-mode validate success now passes through `CheckSuccessBody`; `TestValidateSuccessAdmitsEveryMode` drives staged/live/archive successes. The round-2 anomaly below is resolved, not decided: the document's own success-body list settles it.\\n- FIX (B2): `TestClosedMemberSetsAreDerivedFromSpec` now compares the Members gate map as a set against the derived list for all four tail bodies (success, failure, manifest, doctor); the `manifestMembers` local is renamed `derivedManifest` so it cannot shadow the production map; the log reports member-map comparisons (20 across 21 bodies; SupportedContractVersions has no production gate map by design).\\n- FIX (B3): new `TestRefusalConstructorsMatchProduction` derives the constructor denominator from production — every `axerror.New` site must sit inside a registered constructor body, and the registered set must equal the error-constructing vars exactly. The inventory header sentence now states what both gates do.\\n- FIX (N4): new `TestCheckCallBindingZeroFactsRefuse` — all five `CheckCallBinding` zero-fact exemptions refuse through their own arms.\\n- FIX (N5): `vocabularyTablesInFile` handles shared and paired multi-name initializers (synthetic vectors added); the tagless-switch exemption is confined to `readUTF16Escape` by function name (`classifySwitch` + `TestSwitchClassifierNamesItsExemption`); the census stated bound now names the function-local obligation lists (pinned behaviourally, both directions) and the const/regexp shapes (absent from production).\\n- EVIDENCE: narrowing-mutant battery over the rework scope, every mutant grep-confirmed present and compiling before its verdict; full gates green (see the attached rework-evidence note).\\n\\n### 0444 — Session-adapter leaf rework: all four blocking verdict findings closed, one anomaly reported\\n\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 6561,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1641,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
