{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e0ad","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07545-b24a-7111-bd71-a49bf0fc5a97"},"sequence":3761,"recorded_at":1780531400007517,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e61bb3fc-6388-408f-a265-e94b890e4ba1","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e61bb3fc-6388-408f-a265-e94b890e4ba1","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e61bb3fc-6388-408f-a265-e94b890e4ba1"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"91eaa4f0-452f-457e-99a9-fc51e78c237a"},"task_id":"91eaa4f0-452f-457e-99a9-fc51e78c237a","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"91eaa4f0-452f-457e-99a9-fc51e78c237a","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 6-8\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-## 2026-09-06\n-\n-### 0618 — Session-adapter leaf round-4 rework: rev3 B4/B5/B6 closed as classes, N6 fixed in code\n+## 2026-09-06\n+\n+### 0930 — Directory-node leaf: `internal/dirnode` implemented with enumerated census first\n+\n+- SCOPE: TASK-260830-ljkj8r (second leaf of STORY-260830-3drr2m). New package `internal/dirnode`: two-major manifest bootstrap, envelope framing, manifest/probe/scan/Directory-Query framing, façade host checks, Structured Error 1.2.0 refusals. Six traceability rows (88 → 94), README paragraph. Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\n+- CENSUS FIRST: the leaf-1 lesson (seven rounds, one repeating mistake class) is applied before the battery, not after. `census_test.go` enumerates 10 of 10 AST shapes carrying an error construction (literal, binary-expr with rendered key, constructor registration, New-outside-body, New-as-value, ctor alias in every position, closure-hidden call, aliased import, frameFault literal) with synthetic proofs and named residue. Result: 147 derived arms (145 witnessed + 2 defensive), 8 constructors. The census caught 5 missing witness rows and 3 vacuous fixture vectors during authoring.\n+- NO-OP-PROOF VECTORS: every fixture-surgery site uses `replaceOnce`, which fails when the needle is absent — a mutation that changes nothing can no longer pass against a still-valid body.\n+- FINDINGS: (1) §10.8.5 prose names `query_cursor_mismatch` but the pinned error registry does not register it — cursor reuse refuses as `query_invalid` with a cursor-mismatch detail. (2) The response envelope carries its own `schema` + `schema_version` (1.0.0 both majors): the downgrade tuple names a response schema_version no schemaless reading can carry. (3) `node manifest is not canonical JSON` is reachable, not defensive: extensions values cross opaquely while the canonicalizer enforces depth 256 (300-deep vector proves it). (4) `failCapability` removed — no entry point in this deliverable raises `capability_unavailable`; the taxonomy test pins the 8 emitted codes instead of keeping a dead constructor for census symmetry.\n+- EVIDENCE: narrowing-mutant battery M1–M8, all killed, 0 survivors (M1 downgrade-retryable, M2 v1-macos, M3 conditional-upgrade, M4 scan-replay, M5 index-contiguity, M6 relabeled-schema-version, M7 reasonless-capability, M8 aliased-import with full behavioral suite green). Every mutant copy-aside/copy-back with `cmp` clean; exit codes unpiped. Census-only kills (M8's 4) scored separately.\n+- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (18 pkgs), `-count=3` and `-race` on dirnode exit 0, `-race` on traceability+tracecheck exit 0, `go vet ./...` and `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (acceptance_cases=94). Full-repo `-race` not run (exceeds one bounded call; raced every touched package instead). Dirnode cover 75.0%.\n+- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off uncommitted.\n+\n+### 0618 — Session-adapter leaf round-4 rework: rev3 B4/B5/B6 closed as classes, N6 fixed in code\n"}}}
